From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:11:48 +0000
Subject: Use the ads site setting for new allowed sites

Sites where ads are not blocked can be added in two places: Allowed
sites in the ad blocking settings, which kept its own list, and the
per-site ads setting in Site settings and page info, which the ad
blocker also honors. A site added on the Allowed sites page now goes to
the ads site setting, so a site allowed in any place shows in Site
settings and on the Allowed sites page alike.

The Allowed sites page lists the sites allowed in the ads site setting,
each with its exact address pattern, and the sites added there by an
earlier version. The earlier ones are marked "From an earlier version",
work exactly as before and stay until they are removed. Nothing is
moved or changed on its own. Each row removes only itself. While a
policy sets ads for all sites, nothing can be added there.

A typed site is accepted only if it names a site: a name with a dot,
"localhost", or an IP address. It is allowed with its subdomains, an IP
address exactly.

The setting is named "Ads" in Site settings and page info instead of
"Intrusive ads", with the states "Allowed" and "Blocked". While ads are
blocked by default and no site has its own block, the Ads page in Site
settings only lists sites: the ad blocking settings hold the switch for
all sites. Otherwise the page keeps its setting for all sites, which
now says that sites with their own setting keep it.

